// Fixes the "Filaments" catalog (which was scraped from a German site and
// left German words baked into the base/English columns) and backfills
// proper translations for all 6 storefront locales (en, de, it, fr, nl, es).
//
// Strategy: the base English columns get cleaned (German words swapped for
// English), the ORIGINAL (pre-fix) text is preserved as the "de" translation
// (it was accurate German already), and it/fr/nl/es are generated by
// substituting the same German tokens with their translation in each
// language, then re-running the short_description/description templates in
// that language. Proper-noun marketing names (e.g. "Galaxy", "Basic Black",
// "NFC", "Fiberon", "High Speed") are brand-specific and stay in Latin
// script across all storefronts, matching how every filament brand markets
// these colorways internationally.
//
// IMPORTANT: this script is safe to re-run. It always reads the source text
// from translations.de (the preserved, never-mutated German original) rather
// than from the base columns, which this script itself overwrites. That
// makes every run idempotent and lets a wider dictionary or a word-boundary
// fix repair previously-corrupted output without needing to restore a
// backup: German nouns inflect (Weiß/Weiße/Weißer), so a naive substring
// swap can wreck an unrelated English word that happens to contain a German
// token as a substring (e.g. "Natur" inside "Natural" -> "Naturalal", "Weiß"
// inside "Weiße" -> "Whitee"). translateText() now only swaps a dictionary
// key when it is not glued to another letter on either side, and inflected
// phrases (e.g. "Weiße Eiche", "Schwarze Walnuss") are listed whole so they
// never fall through to the base-word entry.
//
// Run with: npx tsx scripts/localize-filaments.ts
import { db } from "../lib/db"
